+// A PAID provider's on-chain sends (EnclaveConnectivity setHost and qualify, network/onchain-qualification.mjs) under
+// paidFinality "derived" (attested-authority.mjs providerPaidFinality). Every fact a send depends on is taken at an
+// L1-FINALIZED DERIVED Base block, never at the sequencer-signed unsafe head:
+//   * the block: ONE network/lifecycle-finality-bridge.mjs snapshot per operation, over the IN-PROCESS derived reader
+//     capability (network/derived-reader: tier l1-finalized-derived, bounded age, a durable floor that refuses a rollback or
+//     a contradiction - derived-anchor-floor.mjs); the executor's header at that number must be exactly the derived hash,
+//     state root and timestamp, before and after the read;
+//   * state (nonce, simulation, gas search, balance, contract reads): the proof executor - the branded attested verifier or
+//     the local loopback verifier, chosen by chainAuthority - pinned to { blockHash: the derived hash };
+//   * a receipt: the history source names only WHERE (a location hint). Its block M must be the derived block B or an
+//     ancestor whose hash is proven at B (EIP-2935 history storage slot M % 8191, read by the executor pinned to B);
+//     keccak(RLP) of M's header must be that hash; M's transaction bodies (ordinary eth_getBlockByNumber(M, true)) are
+//     re-encoded to their EIP-2718 bytes, each must hash to its body's hash and together they must reproduce M's
+//     transactionsRoot (so a receipt's index is THIS transaction's); the receipts trie, blooms and gas total recomputed by
+//     network/op-receipts-root.mjs must be M's receiptsRoot. Status, gas used and logs come only from that verified data.
+//     A wrong or unknown encoding cannot reproduce the root: it refuses (fails closed), it never resolves.
+//
+// THE NONCE JOURNAL (durable, contiguous, exclusively owned - a kernel lock beside the file). The next nonce is P, the nonce
+// PROVEN at the derived block, plus the number of this provider's own recorded, exact-byte transactions at or above P - never
+// a backend's word. Each signed transaction is written durably BEFORE its broadcast and is only ever re-broadcast as the same
+// bytes. At each derived block:
+//   * an entry below P resolves: by a receipt proven as above (success or revert), else as "nonce consumed" (proven at
+//     finality, not landed by this send) - never as success;
+//   * the journal's first remaining entry must be exactly P: anything else is a gap or a contradiction (refused, nothing
+//     pruned, nothing signed - settle it by hand);
+//   * the own backend's pending nonce is only a GATE: above P + own entries = a transaction of this key nobody recorded
+//     (refused); below = the pool lost own bytes (re-broadcast unchanged, signing waits for the pool to hold them).
+// Several sends can therefore be pending at once (bounded by maxPending), each awaiting its own proof. A call identical to a
+// pending one (same to and data) returns that pending hash instead of being signed again. What pipelining does NOT give:
+// a simulation and the balance check run at B and ignore this provider's own pending transactions (the balance covers all
+// of their maximum costs together); a later transaction that depends on an earlier pending one can still revert at the head
+// (reported as reverted). Final success always waits for a derived anchor covering the block (L1 finality plus derivation).
+//
+// The operator's OWN Base node (cfg.txBackend) is never evidence: chain id, its header at B (must hash to the derived hash),
+// the pending-nonce gate, the tip hint (capped), and eth_sendRawTransaction. History bytes come from the optional private
+// read-only historyUrl (else from the own backend's eth namespace): eth_chainId, eth_getTransactionReceipt (hint),
+// eth_getBlockByNumber, eth_getBlockReceipts - every byte checked as above. No debug namespace is used.
+import fs from 'node:fs';
+import path from 'node:path';
+import { encodeFunctionData, keccak256, hexToBytes, bytesToHex, parseTransaction, recoverTransactionAddress, getAddress, serializeTransaction } from 'viem';
+import { verifierEndpoint } from '../verified-chain.mjs';
+import { createLifecycleFinalitySnapshot } from '../lifecycle-finality-bridge.mjs';
